entries.description:
Entries, one destination each: a host name, `*.suffix`, an IP address
or a CIDR prefix, then optionally `:` and ports (`443,8000-8100`;
`443` when absent).

match_mode.description:
Execution mode: `"full"`/omitted runs the script once over the whole scope;
`"span"` runs it once per `trigger_regex` match on just the matched span.
`"span"` requires a non-blank `trigger_regex`.

client_name.description:
Optional human-readable client name. RFC 7591 calls this optional;
we substitute `"unnamed-dcr-client"` when absent so the admin UI has
something to render.

EgressSettings.description:
Every surface's list. An entry is `*` (every private address), an IP
address, a CIDR prefix (`10.0.0.0/8`) or a host name (that exact name);
an empty list reaches no private address.

entities.description:
Distinct PII entity types found on this step (e.g. `["US_SSN",
"EMAIL_ADDRESS"]`). Set only on PII findings (`name == "guardrail:pii"`);
`None` on injection-classifier steps.

KeyListItem.description:
One row of the unified key inventory — gateway keys (`api_keys`) and
automation keys (`automation_keys`) in a single shape. `kind` discriminates;
per-family fields are `null` where they don't apply.

standalone.description:
Inheritance mode: `false` = Layered (inherits the Default + own diff);
`true` = Standalone (owns its full content). The Default profile is
standalone (it is the base).

has_backend.description:
`true` iff the admin has selected a search backend in
`system_settings.web`. False means only `web_fetch` is served;
`web_search` appears once a backend is configured.

