client_secret.description:
The client secret, when the server issued a confidential client. Absent
for public (PKCE-only) clients. Returned once for the operator to save;
this endpoint persists nothing.

oneOf.description:
Nothing was written. `missing` names the bodies the share did not
carry and admin-api does not hold — resend them with the records;
empty for a transient failure.

tenant_budget_mode.description:
`"enforce"` (default) rejects a request once the org total is over cap;
`"alert_only"` keeps accruing and still fires the crossing notification,
without blocking.

ToolsChangeKind.description:
Kind of `ToolsChanged` event. `between_turns` signals the available tool
set differs from the previous turn (client added/removed/swapped tools);
`policy_modified` signals tool policy mutated the set on this turn.

items.description:
One row of the unified key inventory — gateway keys (`api_keys`) and
automation keys (`automation_keys`) in a single shape. `kind` discriminates;
per-family fields are `null` where they don't apply.

oneOf.description:
When present, replaces the key's budget triple (daily/monthly/mode);
omit to leave the budget untouched. A present object with null caps
clears the per-key budget.

UpdateMcpCatalogEntry.description:
Request body for editing a catalog entry. Omitted fields are unchanged and
`null` or `""` clears an optional text field;
editing a built-in flips it to a user entry so seed-sync stops overwriting it.

UpdatePricingSettingsRequest.description:
Body for `PATCH /api/v1/admin/settings/pricing`. Both fields are optional;
`fx` replaces the table wholesale, because an operator edits a rate table as
one document and a per-pair merge would leave stale pairs behind invisibly.

profile_id.description:
Transform profile scope (tri-state PATCH): absent → unchanged; `null` →
**shared** (the Default transform profile, the base every profile reads);
a profile id → **specific** to that transform profile.
